WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.314
Evil Grimace

00:00:00.314 --> 00:00:05.601
was born on June 12, 1971, a day that will now live in infamy forever.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.026
This is also the date, according to representatives at McDonald's,

00:00:08.058 --> 00:00:09.722
that Grimace starred in his first commercial.

00:00:09.786 --> 00:00:12.602
Looking back at these early commercials, Grimace is played for a fool.

00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:16.138
But make no mistake, there is more to this purple blob of evil than meets

00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:16.602
the eye.

00:00:16.602 --> 00:00:19.706
In the early 70s, Grimace started off as one of the three main antagonists

00:00:19.738 --> 00:00:22.878
of Ronald McDonald lore, stealing shakes and Coca Cola from children.

00:00:22.964 --> 00:00:25.686
He doesn't seem to be in league with the other antagonist, such as the

00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:29.266
Hamburglar, who fittingly stole hamburgers, or Captain Crook, who bizarrely

00:00:29.298 --> 00:00:30.850
only stole the filet of fish.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.270
Captain Crook did not survive past the 1980s, so do with that information

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:35.990
what you will.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.854
While the Hamburglar, disturbing in his own right, was certainly the most

00:00:38.892 --> 00:00:42.082
infamous of the three, it would be Grimace who persevered as a modern horror.

00:00:42.146 --> 00:00:45.738
What is Grimace? Where did he come from? And how did he become the

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:50.467
face of the scandal that allegedly killed hundreds, no, thousands of teens in 2023? 

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:55.178
What is in the Grimace shake? The answers may cause you to Grimace.

00:00:55.274 --> 00:00:58.400
For all of that and more, stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.673
🎵 Metal Music 🎵

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.886
At first, I was like Charles Entertainment Cheese was likely born sometime

00:01:07.918 --> 00:01:13.310
in the early 1970s as a joke, but, bro, I don't think it's a joke anymore.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:14.658
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:14.744 --> 00:01:17.378
You may think that the recent wave of reports about a Grimace would be the

00:01:17.384 --> 00:01:20.462
first time that McDonald's lore crossed over here onto my horror channel.

00:01:20.536 --> 00:01:21.174
No, it's not.

00:01:21.212 --> 00:01:24.130
Other than that offhand remark I made in my Billy Hargrove analysis.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.834
Or what if it caused him to slowly turn into Grimace from the McDonald's commercial? 

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.426
Let's not forget that Pennywise's infamous interaction with

00:01:30.448 --> 00:01:33.690
Georgie is based off of an early commercial with Ronald McDonald.

00:01:34.176 --> 00:01:37.117
-[Ronald McDonald] Well hi! Isn't that McDonald's hamburger delicious? 

00:01:37.288 --> 00:01:39.746
-[Kid]  Mom told me never to talk to strangers.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:48.506
-[IT] Hi, Georgie. Don't you want a balloon? 
-[Georgie] I'm not supposed to take stuff from strangers.

00:01:48.618 --> 00:01:52.117
The McDonald's characters are more closely tied to horror than you may have thought.

00:01:52.117 --> 00:01:55.194
From urban legends about the mascots to one of the all time classic

00:01:55.242 --> 00:01:58.634
creepypastas Ronald McDonald house, to this set of alleged Japanese

00:01:58.682 --> 00:02:01.600
McDonald's commercials uploaded to YouTube in 2015.

00:02:15.923 --> 00:02:18.237
[Ronald McDonald] McDonalds.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:19.994
There's no way that's real.

00:02:20.032 --> 00:02:23.130
But whoever made this made it specifically for my sense of humor.

00:02:28.584 --> 00:02:30.164
-[Ronald McDonald] McDonald's. 

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.334
But we're not here to talk about Ronald.

00:02:33.382 --> 00:02:35.034
We're here to talk about Grimace.

00:02:35.082 --> 00:02:38.206
I've always thought Grimace was a creepy character as is, but as we look

00:02:38.228 --> 00:02:40.138
back in time, it gets even worse.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:43.322
The original commercial portrayed Grimace as a dopey but crazed addict

00:02:43.386 --> 00:02:44.970
living in a cave with four arms.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:48.018
However, this was actually a less scary version of Grimace than what they

00:02:48.024 --> 00:02:49.202
had originally come up with.

00:02:49.256 --> 00:02:52.926
In a 2012 interview with QSR magazine, former McDonald's VP of advertising

00:02:52.958 --> 00:02:54.026
Roy T. Bergold said

00:02:54.026 --> 00:02:57.266
the original Grimace was scaly, mean looking, had four arms,

00:02:57.298 --> 00:02:59.026
and had no charm whatsoever.

00:02:59.138 --> 00:03:03.030
In the first ad campaign, he's literally referred to as the Evil Grimace.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:09.474
-[Commercial VO] It was a gloomy day in McDonald's land because the evil Grimace

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.710
-[Commercial VO] had grabbed all the cups.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.386
But over the years, the character transitioned into the softer, plush, two

00:03:15.408 --> 00:03:16.778
armed blob that we know today.

00:03:16.864 --> 00:03:20.086
But despite the more unnerving aspects being kicked down a notch, there's

00:03:20.118 --> 00:03:23.406
still something very disturbing about Grimace if we dig into the details of

00:03:23.428 --> 00:03:23.928
his lore.

00:03:23.962 --> 00:03:27.338
But to fully understand Grimace, we've got to take it back to his homeland

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.150
and his people.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.494
Yeah, there's more

00:03:30.532 --> 00:03:31.310
than one Grimace.

