when you can just go outside and pick all of the same items for free.

00:07:47.332 --> 00:07:50.834
So when did Grimace first appear in McDonald land? There is a 1981

00:07:50.872 --> 00:07:52.526
commercial about how Ronald met Grimace when they were babies. 

00:07:52.558 --> 00:07:55.454
Grimace was in a runaway baby carriage, which Ronald

00:07:55.502 --> 00:07:58.978
helped stop by offering him a bag of McDonald's, and they became friends.

00:07:59.064 --> 00:08:02.354
However, as we know, that's not what Grimace even looked like as a baby.

00:08:02.402 --> 00:08:05.942
This is clearly a PR move by McDonald's corporate trying to rewrite history

00:08:05.996 --> 00:08:08.966
and cover up the way they treated the evil Grimace in the early going.

00:08:09.068 --> 00:08:12.326
As we know, Grimace's earliest appearances portrayed him as a cave dwelling

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.506
monster who steals shakes and cola from children.

00:08:14.608 --> 00:08:18.134
However, early Grimace is easily outwitted by Ronald, who uses a disguise.

00:08:18.182 --> 00:08:21.606
And really, who would be fooled by this disguise?

00:08:21.638 --> 00:08:22.294
It's literally just a hat and a mailbag.

00:08:22.342 --> 00:08:25.046
But it's enough to convince Grimace that he's been selected for a beauty contest.

00:08:25.078 --> 00:08:28.398
You know, Grimace, I hate to be the one to tell you this, but if

00:08:28.404 --> 00:08:32.078
you look like this and someone says you've won a beauty contest, it's a

00:08:32.084 --> 00:08:33.582
scam. It's a scam Grimace.

00:08:33.646 --> 00:08:36.098
Then he basically falls for the same trick again. When this happens.

00:08:36.184 --> 00:08:41.442
-[Commercial] Ronald and his friends spotted evil Grimace running off

00:08:41.496 --> 00:08:44.350
-[Commercial] with loads of shakes and fries.
-[Grimace] Feisty.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:48.894
-[Commercial] Thinking quickly, Ronald disguised himself as a big Hollywood movie director.

00:08:48.942 --> 00:08:52.006
Ronald claims he's going to make the evil Grimace a star and

00:08:52.028 --> 00:08:53.682
tricks him into falling into a lake.

00:08:53.746 --> 00:08:57.602
But by the time we next see Grimace in 1973, things have changed.

00:08:57.666 --> 00:09:01.362
He's no longer referred to as the Evil Grimace, but rather just The Grimace,

00:09:01.426 --> 00:09:03.682
which to me sounds like ten times more horrifying.

00:09:03.746 --> 00:09:06.778
He's also lost his second set of arms and seems to now be friends with

00:09:06.784 --> 00:09:07.654
Ronald and the gang.

00:09:07.702 --> 00:09:10.746
It's not clear to me if losing arms is part of the aging process for Grimaces,

00:09:10.768 --> 00:09:13.658
like how we lose our baby teeth, or if this was a result of the

00:09:13.664 --> 00:09:16.974
McDonald's corporation torturing and experimenting on him to create

00:09:17.012 --> 00:09:17.930
a kid friendly mascot.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.606
The latter would not surprise me, given what we learned from this commercial.

00:09:20.628 --> 00:09:23.418
Grimace is headed to the beach to do some tanning, but the heat

00:09:23.434 --> 00:09:27.086
of the sun causes him to literally deflate, shrivel, and dry out, and they

00:09:27.108 --> 00:09:29.746
have to feed him McDonald's shakes in order to essentially rehydrate him

00:09:29.768 --> 00:09:30.418
back to health.

00:09:30.504 --> 00:09:33.774
So in the previous commercials, where they steal back the shakes and drinks

00:09:33.822 --> 00:09:36.386
from him, they were actually putting him at risk of having some kind of

00:09:36.408 --> 00:09:37.550
major medical episode.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:41.206
This commercial also has a brief cameo from Huggy the Tree, who may be even

00:09:41.228 --> 00:09:44.486
more creepy than Ronald or Grimace, but we'll get back to him in a little bit.

00:09:44.508 --> 00:09:47.686
Throughout the early 70s, the citizens, or whatever you want to

00:09:47.708 --> 00:09:50.674
call them, of McDonald Land were starting to skyrocket with fame.

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:53.594
As a result, the McDonald's corporation integrated the characters into

00:09:53.632 --> 00:09:57.398
restaurants with areas known as McDonald's Playlands, and in 1976, Grimace

00:09:57.414 --> 00:09:59.590
and the others were even developed into action figures.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:01.450
These were horrifying in their own right.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.418
I don't know why Ronald has black eyes.

00:10:03.504 --> 00:10:06.602
I don't know how Huggy the tree manages to look even creepier.

00:10:06.666 --> 00:10:09.082
And Grimace's status of an action figure is debatable.

00:10:09.146 --> 00:10:12.190
The only part of him that moved was the fur, giving him a completely

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:15.338
different and somehow unsettling feel from the other characters.

00:10:15.434 --> 00:10:18.686
It also became an annual tradition for Grimace to celebrate his birthday at McDonald's.

00:10:18.708 --> 00:10:21.858
In these photos, we can see what appears to be a rare glimpse of

00:10:21.864 --> 00:10:24.818
Grimace's mother, suggesting the possibility of more Grimaces on the

00:10:24.824 --> 00:10:27.138
mainland, some of whom we would meet before long.

00:10:27.224 --> 00:10:32.118
But in 1977, disaster struck McDonald Land when Mayor McCheese was sued for

00:10:32.124 --> 00:10:35.654
his resemblance to the children's show HR Pufnstuf, and had to step down

00:10:35.692 --> 00:10:37.014
from holding political office.

00:10:37.132 --> 00:10:40.626
At this time, many other citizens were forced to rethink their life of fame,

00:10:40.658 --> 00:10:44.234
and Officer Big Mac, Captain Crook, and The Professor chose to step back

00:10:44.272 --> 00:10:47.274
from the limelight and end their careers as commercial performers to live

00:10:47.312 --> 00:10:48.742
quiet lives of solitude.

00:10:48.806 --> 00:10:52.266
Grimace, however, chose to continue making McDonald Land commercials, even

00:10:52.288 --> 00:10:54.630
moving to Malibu when he got his license at age 16.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:58.606
In 1978, the world was introduced to Uncle O'Grimacey, a green variant of Grimace,

00:10:58.628 --> 00:11:01.690
who helped promote the Shamrock Shake and also appeared on the cup.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:04.922
Near the beginning of the 80s, Grimace got braces and grew out a mullet,

00:11:04.986 --> 00:11:08.094
which raises some serious questions about how his hair growth and grooming

00:11:08.142 --> 00:11:08.946
routine works.

00:11:09.048 --> 00:11:12.690
One of the most horrifying iterations of Grimace would have to be in 1984.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:15.854
It seems as if the Hamburglar had recently had some work done to appear

00:11:15.902 --> 00:11:19.406
younger, and Grimace, perhaps in an effort to keep up, gets this very creepy

00:11:19.438 --> 00:11:21.810
lip job giving the appearance of human lips.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:23.611
This is also something I talked about in my

00:11:23.611 --> 00:11:24.412
Chuck E. Cheese video.

00:11:24.412 --> 00:11:26.599
The human lips on a children's entertainment character be

00:11:26.599 --> 00:11:28.014
will never not creepy 

00:11:28.014 --> 00:11:29.670
like A Trip to the Moon (1902)

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:30.982
That should have been the end of it.

00:11:31.036 --> 00:11:34.326
Another thing I always find creepy is mixing animation styles, and that's

00:11:34.358 --> 00:11:37.626
exactly what would happen with Grimace and the gang next in 1998, when they

00:11:37.648 --> 00:11:41.470
starred in the documentary series The Wacky Adventures of Ronald McDonald.

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:53.386
Are we sure they're not doing this on purpose? This was a series of VHS

00:11:53.418 --> 00:11:56.714
tapes given out with Happy Meals, and one of the episodes focuses on Grimace's

00:11:56.762 --> 00:11:58.202
homecoming to Grimace Island.

00:11:58.266 --> 00:12:01.426
It starts with Ronald receiving a video call from Grimace about a letter he

00:12:01.448 --> 00:12:03.730
received inviting him to come home and help out his people.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:06.878
And can I just point out how during this call, Grimace's video feed is

00:12:06.904 --> 00:12:10.422
constantly glitching, like some kind of analog horror found footage?

00:12:10.476 --> 00:12:13.720
Just keep that in mind, as it would become kind of a trend for him.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.054
-[Commercial] Oh, boy.

00:12:16.252 --> 00:12:24.090
-[Commercial] At the edge of a universe, humming a tune for merely dreaming.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.466
Birdie and Hamburglar call in as well, but they don't glitch out nearly as

00:12:27.488 --> 00:12:28.410
much as Grimace does.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.786
The rest of the episode switches to a Rugrat style, and they set sail,

00:12:31.808 --> 00:12:33.482
not realizing they're being tailed by pirates.

00:12:33.546 --> 00:12:37.050
Grimace doesn't quite know how to get there until Hamburglar finds the map.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.617
-[Hamburglar) Hey, what's that in your pocket, Grimace?

00:12:39.617 --> 00:12:45.098
Hold up. Grimace is not wearing any clothing, therefore he does not have any pockets.

00:12:45.194 --> 00:12:48.162
I personally would not be reaching into a Grimace like that.

00:12:48.216 --> 00:12:50.194
I mean, that's a little...

00:12:50.312 --> 00:12:53.154
So everyone touches the map, and it basically says that they have to go

00:12:53.192 --> 00:12:54.802
straight through this channel that they're going through.

00:12:54.856 --> 00:12:57.778
So after getting whale yeeted, going through a storm, and also having to

00:12:57.784 --> 00:13:00.966
battle a King Kraken, they get sucked into a whirlpool that spits them out

00:13:00.988 --> 00:13:03.686
in this underground cavern under Grimace Island, where there are just

00:13:03.708 --> 00:13:05.830
Grimaces huddled in the shadows, watching them.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.250
Absolutely terrifying.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:10.214
However, when they see one of their own kind, they celebrate, but later

00:13:10.252 --> 00:13:12.642
scold him for bringing illegal aliens across the border.

00:13:12.706 --> 00:13:15.953
They're all forced to team up, though, when the pirates attack seeking the treasure. 

00:13:15.953 --> 00:13:18.586
The Pirates blast raw fish at the Grimaces, which seems to be

00:13:18.608 --> 00:13:19.222
their weakness.

00:13:19.286 --> 00:13:22.170
And I have a theory about why, which I'll get into in a little bit.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:25.110
But in the end, Grimace leads the charge of bravery against the pirates, and

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:28.206
he's awarded with a piece of treasure, a golden cup, calling back to his

00:13:28.228 --> 00:13:30.906
first ever appearance, where he's addicted to collecting shake and cola cups.

00:13:30.938 --> 00:13:34.394
During the ending segment, Grimace shares a montage of the Grimace

00:13:34.442 --> 00:13:37.714
home movies, which is exactly the kind of nightmare fuel you'd expect, but

00:13:37.752 --> 00:13:40.882
also showing us a rare glimpse of Grimace's parents, grandmother, and

00:13:40.936 --> 00:13:44.018
greatgrandmother, which begins to raise the question of how long does a

00:13:44.024 --> 00:13:47.106
Grimace live? The trend of introducing family members would continue in a

00:13:47.128 --> 00:13:50.166
commercial the next year, when Grimace's, Aunts Millie and Tilly show up at

00:13:50.188 --> 00:13:50.946
a burger picnic.

00:13:50.978 --> 00:13:54.502
The wacky adventures of Ronald McDonald ended in 2003, and after this,

00:13:54.556 --> 00:13:57.410
Grimace disappeared from the public eye for almost a decade.

00:13:57.490 --> 00:14:00.470
This gave people time to reflect on his rise and fall, and the questions

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.530
started cropping up.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:06.149
What exactly is a Grimace? I mean, Mayor McCheese was obviously a Cheeseburger, 

00:14:06.149 --> 00:14:08.618
Birdie is a McChicken, and they're even talking McNuggets and

00:14:08.624 --> 00:14:09.382
trash bins.

00:14:09.446 --> 00:14:13.566
But what facet of McDonald's was Grimace born to represent? The answer was

00:14:13.588 --> 00:14:17.070
about to come out, and it would be truly horrifying.

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:21.372
(IMPACT)

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.298
-[CBS News] Forget Blogging and MySpace.

00:14:24.394 --> 00:14:28.334
-[CBS News] If you really want to stay connected, there is a new service, 

00:14:28.382 --> 00:14:30.066
-[CBS News] and supposedly it is the next big thing.

00:14:30.168 --> 00:14:31.918
-[CBS News] It's a name you can't forget.

00:14:32.014 --> 00:14:35.458
With social media making it easier than ever for fandoms to connect online,

00:14:35.544 --> 00:14:38.302
people began to speculate about what happened to Grimace.

00:14:38.366 --> 00:14:41.526
Other than a rumored appearance at a Dodger game in 2012, he seems to have

00:14:41.548 --> 00:14:43.158
just vanished from public life.

00:14:43.244 --> 00:14:46.774
Had he retired? Was he dead? Was the McDonald's corporation keeping him quiet?

00:14:46.812 --> 00:14:50.166
Well, ironically, it would be the McDonald's Corporation that would

00:14:50.188 --> 00:14:52.842
break the silence on Twitter in May 2012.

00:14:52.976 --> 00:14:56.938
Grimace is the embodiment of a milkshake, though others still insist he's a

00:14:56.944 --> 00:14:57.590
taste bud.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:00.710
So the two options here are rather grim.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:04.286
Either he's a milkshake who loves drinking milkshakes, thus making the

00:15:04.308 --> 00:15:08.526
Grimace's cannibals, or he's a taste bud, which means any bodily contact you

00:15:08.548 --> 00:15:10.942
have with him is him tasting you.

00:15:11.076 --> 00:15:12.250
Don't touch Grimace.

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:16.574
This idea gives a disturbing new context to scenes of Grimace past.

00:15:16.612 --> 00:15:19.614
During the trip to Grimace Island, when Ronald surfs on top of Grimace.

00:15:19.662 --> 00:15:22.994
He's laughing in a bliss and delight, not because it tickles, but because he

00:15:23.032 --> 00:15:25.326
enjoys the way that Ronald tastes.

00:15:25.438 --> 00:15:28.834
Number 15 McDonald's foot Grimace.

00:15:28.962 --> 00:15:32.226
Remember those chairs that children would sit on in the McDonald's Play Place?

00:15:32.258 --> 00:15:34.774
Bros literally drooling? Of course.

00:15:34.812 --> 00:15:38.578
The Grimace themed addition to those Play Places are literally a child cage.

00:15:38.674 --> 00:15:41.042
Can't let them get away before Grimace gets a taste.

00:15:41.106 --> 00:15:43.606
And if you think about it, the scene with the pirates shooting the dead fish

00:15:43.638 --> 00:15:46.714
at the Grimaces, and that seemingly being their weakness makes sense because

00:15:46.752 --> 00:15:49.638
being taste buds, they wouldn't like to make contact with rotting fish.

00:15:49.734 --> 00:15:53.066
Speculation continued to swirl for several years, but Grimace still did not

00:15:53.088 --> 00:15:56.426
make an appearance until 2020, when he got out to the

00:15:56.458 --> 00:15:57.790
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade in New York City.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:00.954
The science is still not settled on whether or not a Grimace can get COVID.

00:16:01.002 --> 00:16:04.766
But a year later, the science on what exactly a Grimace is would be

00:16:04.788 --> 00:16:08.386
confirmed when Brian Bates, a McDonald's manager in Windsor, Canada, did an

00:16:08.408 --> 00:16:12.222
interview where he was asked what a Grimace is, he told them, and I quote,

00:16:12.286 --> 00:16:15.662
he is an enormous taste bud, but a taste bud nonetheless.

00:16:15.806 --> 00:16:17.746
This sent the Internet into a frenzy.

00:16:17.848 --> 00:16:19.626
My entire world has been upended.

00:16:19.678 --> 00:16:22.694
I mean, I never knew what the hell Grimace was, but I didn't think it was this.

00:16:22.732 --> 00:16:26.886
Another user chillingly noted, Grimace can taste with his whole body.

00:16:26.988 --> 00:16:29.202
But perhaps the best point came from this woman.

00:16:29.266 --> 00:16:32.394
If Grimace is a taste bud, why on earth would you name the damn thing after

00:16:32.432 --> 00:16:35.926
an expression of disgust? But the confirmation of Grimace as a taste bud

00:16:35.958 --> 00:16:38.298
starts to make other Grimace mysteries make more sense.

00:16:38.384 --> 00:16:41.018
Primarily, the whole understanding that seemed to be reached between the

00:16:41.024 --> 00:16:44.458
Evil Grimace and the McDonald's corporation around 1973.

00:16:44.544 --> 00:16:47.738
McDonald's would stop villainizing the creature, and he would stop stealing

00:16:47.754 --> 00:16:48.602
all of their shakes.

00:16:48.666 --> 00:16:51.534
Instead, he would work for them as a corporate mascot and appear in ad campaigns, 

00:16:51.572 --> 00:16:55.306
which gave him the opportunity to satisfy his hunger by tasting

00:16:55.338 --> 00:16:57.998
the kids in the restaurant during meet and greets and other events.

00:16:58.094 --> 00:17:01.458
This would also explain his disappearance as McDonald's shifted away from

00:17:01.464 --> 00:17:03.598
the Play Place to focus more on drive through orders.

00:17:03.614 --> 00:17:06.594
In the 2000s, Grimace wouldn't have the opportunity to taste as many

00:17:06.632 --> 00:17:09.102
children and thus had no incentive to do the ads.

00:17:09.166 --> 00:17:12.646
It seems like this discussion of what Grimace is made him nostalgic for his

00:17:12.668 --> 00:17:15.366
days in the spotlight, and he took to the McDonald's twitter account in

00:17:15.388 --> 00:17:19.974
September 2021 to say this - it's always what is Grimace? And never, how is Grimace? 

00:17:20.012 --> 00:17:25.098
Then, in January 2022, Tesla CEO Elon Musk tweeted,

00:17:25.104 --> 00:17:27.894
I will eat a happy meal on TV if McDonald's accepts Dogecoin.

00:17:27.942 --> 00:17:31.466
To which McDonald's, seemingly hijacked by Grimace, again responded, only if

00:17:31.488 --> 00:17:33.094
Tesla accepts Grimace coin.

00:17:33.142 --> 00:17:37.182
As of recording, tesla still does not accept Grimace coin, as far as I know.

00:17:37.236 --> 00:17:39.754
But this tweet got a lot of attention and may have given the McDonald's

00:17:39.802 --> 00:17:42.234
marketing team an idea to bring Grimace out of the dark,

00:17:42.282 --> 00:17:44.318
pun intended, for a new ad campaign.

00:17:44.414 --> 00:17:48.462
In June 2023, it was time to celebrate Grimace's 52nd birthday.

00:17:48.526 --> 00:17:50.930
And that's where things get weird.

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:54.094
-[Commercial] Happy birthday. Surprise.

00:17:54.222 --> 00:17:59.270
-[Commercial] Since he was born, Grimace has always had a birthday.

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:07.582
-[Commercial] And since he's had a birthday, he's always had it at McDonald's.

00:18:07.746 --> 00:18:12.794
-[Commercial] So this June, we're all invited to the party

00:18:12.832 --> 00:18:13.690
-[Commercial] with a special shake to celebrate.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:22.426
Now, I personally have a feeling that McDonald's wanted to leverage the

00:18:22.448 --> 00:18:25.658
creepy aspect of Grimace for their campaign, but wanted to do so in a subtle

00:18:25.674 --> 00:18:27.930
way that doesn't harm their clean company image.

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:31.502
They probably saw the free publicity that the rat in the child casino across

00:18:31.556 --> 00:18:34.446
town was getting when Shane Dawson went all Victor Frankenstein on their

00:18:34.468 --> 00:18:36.766
pizzas and thought they could leverage some of that energy to their advantage.

00:18:36.788 --> 00:18:39.586
If you look closely, the evidence is right there in the commercial.

00:18:39.608 --> 00:18:42.558
The first thing we actually see is the creepiest McDonald's

00:18:42.574 --> 00:18:45.410
character Huggy the tree, and he appears again later in the ad.

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.850
Add in the fact that they use old photos, it's commonly known that any media

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:50.382
plus time can equal creepy.

00:18:50.446 --> 00:18:53.366
Then, when Grimace skates into the McDonald's on its birthday look at this

00:18:53.388 --> 00:18:54.114
girl's reaction.

00:18:54.162 --> 00:18:56.610
I don't know about you, but to me, she looks terrified.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.250
And I guess it's for a good reason.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:01.546
Ever since the Grimace shake became available, TikTok has been filled with

00:19:01.568 --> 00:19:05.034
people, mostly teenagers, toasting the purple big boy, sipping the shake and

00:19:05.072 --> 00:19:07.050
suffering disturbing reactions.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.894
Again, this is probably a case of any publicity as good publicity, because

00:19:18.932 --> 00:19:23.006
even as these videos gain more traction with now over 1.3 billion views on

00:19:23.028 --> 00:19:25.826
the hashtag GrimaceShake alone, the beverage seems to be growing in popularity.

00:19:25.848 --> 00:19:30.062
Which leaves the question, what exactly is in the Grimace shake?

00:19:30.126 --> 00:19:33.246
According to McDonald's themselves, the delicious Grimace's birthday shake

00:19:33.278 --> 00:19:35.870
is inspired by Grimaces's iconic color and sweetness.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:39.622
It features creamy vanilla soft serve, blended with Grimace shake syrup and

00:19:39.676 --> 00:19:41.346
finished with whipped light cream.

00:19:41.458 --> 00:19:45.874
So what about this Grimace shake syrup? The McDonald's website lists several

00:19:45.922 --> 00:19:49.298
ingredients, but offers no clue as to where the syrup comes from or why it's

00:19:49.314 --> 00:19:50.918
called a Grimace shake syrup.

00:19:51.014 --> 00:19:54.138
That's when I realized the answer has been there all along.

00:19:54.224 --> 00:19:57.898
Grimace is the embodiment of a milkshake, though others still insist he's a

00:19:57.904 --> 00:19:58.550
taste bud.

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.746
Maybe that's because he's both.

00:20:00.848 --> 00:20:03.142
He is the taste bud of a living milkshake.

00:20:03.206 --> 00:20:04.246
He likes milkshakes.

00:20:04.278 --> 00:20:07.514
They literally inflate his mass and keep him healthy, and he likes tasting

00:20:07.562 --> 00:20:08.590
everything around him.

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:11.838
Not only does this explain the tweets, but it also explains why some of the

00:20:11.844 --> 00:20:14.586
videos show consumers reacting poorly to the shakes because they're

00:20:14.618 --> 00:20:16.062
literally consuming Grimace matter.

00:20:16.116 --> 00:20:18.322
And some of the videos show Grimace coming after them.

00:20:18.376 --> 00:20:22.354
He simply wants to steal the shakes, just as he had as evil Grimace way back

00:20:22.392 --> 00:20:23.854
at the very beginning.

00:20:23.982 --> 00:20:27.394
But with the success of the Grimace shake and Grimace now out on the loose

00:20:27.442 --> 00:20:28.422
rampaging in public.

00:20:28.476 --> 00:20:32.002
It'll be interesting to see what becomes of Grimace next year on Grimace's birthday.

00:20:32.066 --> 00:20:35.750
-[Commercial] Happy birthday, Grimace.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:47.162
And with that, there's only one thing left for me to do.

00:20:47.216 --> 00:20:50.806
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring the death

00:20:50.838 --> 00:20:54.560
bell and select all notifications, and I will see you in the next one,

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.730
assuming we both survive.

